# armada-interface — local vs deployed

Before editing config, fees, relayer, or deploy files, read **`apps/armada-interface/LOCAL_VS_DEPLOY.md`**.

## Do not change

- **`sepolia` relayer default** — never fall back to `http://localhost:3001` in `network.ts` / `sepoliaConfig()`. Hosted browsers cannot reach localhost.
- **`resolveRelayerUrl()`** — local → localhost when unset; sepolia → empty string when unset.
- **`useFees` / `resolveFeeCacheId`** — when `!isRelayerConfigured()`, use offline fee schedule (`offline-fees`); do not require live `/fees` for wallet-submit flows.
- **`vercel.json`** — keep `build.env.VITE_NETWORK = "sepolia"` for production previews.
- **`netlify.toml`** — keep `VITE_NETWORK = "sepolia"` in `[build.environment]`.

## Safe changes

- Set `VITE_RELAYER_URL` in hosting UI to a **public HTTPS** relayer when available.
- Local-only: `.env.development`, mock balance, Debug drip, `isLocalMode()` UX gates.

## Verify after touching this area

```bash
npm test --workspace=@armada/interface -- --run network.relayer resolveFeeCacheId useFees
```
